body:
If I add a **RouteFilter** as this

```
package io.quarkus;

import io.quarkus.vertx.http.runtime.CurrentVertxRequest;
import io.quarkus.vertx.web.RouteFilter;
import io.vertx.ext.web.RoutingContext;

import javax.inject.Inject;

public class TestFilter {

    @Inject
    private CurrentVertxRequest currentVertxRequest;

    @RouteFilter(100)
    void myFilter(RoutingContext rc) {
        currentVertxRequest.setCurrent(rc);
        rc.next();
    }
}
```

it works but only for GET type calls for reactive routes. I think that we come then to the case described here #13073

```
